      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 402007151,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The change is so big that Gitlab does not render the diff, preventing any kind of review. It needs to be split in smaller chunks so that comments can be made inline.\nOur recommended changeset format is to have a single line with a summary, a empty line and then details. An example would be to split the change in at least 3 parts for example:\nMBIM: add extended version 1.0 commands\nMBIM: add extended version 2.0 commands\nMBIM: add extended version 3.0 commands\n\nThe only thing I had the time to see when downloading the file is that the extende dversion shouold not be a global variable IMHO, but instead a new parameter in the mbim_conv_info conversation structure, like cellular_class for example. Using a global variable prevents the support of several modems in a single pcap.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6722527,
            "username": "pquantin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Pascal Quantin",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9bf49edc6acae0eca821eb90309381794fb4fbea4f3fb7c2378428862ddbb430?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/pquantin"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-08-25T20:20:19.658Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-08-25T21:51:11.382Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 68720039,
